Package name;
The whitelist only needs to pass in the package name;
Blacklist can also be set to specify the id, package name and id separated by ",", multiple ids separated by "-", such as "com.urovo.testdemo,1-2-3 "means hide notifications with id 1, 2 or 3, other ids will be shown normally; if you want to hide all the notifications of the app, just pass in the package name "com.urovo.testdemo";
Whitelisting is preferred;
